{
  "id": "m60l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Montículos con heapq",
    "en": "Heaps with heapq"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Siempre el menor a mano"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Un **montículo** (heap) es una estructura que da acceso rápido al elemento más pequeño. `heapq` trabaja sobre listas normales: `heappush` añade, `heappop` saca SIEMPRE el menor."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import heapq",
          "h = []",
          "heapq.heappush(h, 3)",
          "heapq.heappush(h, 1)",
          "heapq.heappush(h, 2)",
          "print(heapq.heappop(h))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`heapq.nsmallest(n, datos)` y `nlargest(n, datos)` dan los n menores/mayores sin ordenar todo."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Un heap es la base de una cola de prioridad: atender siempre lo más urgente primero."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Always the smallest at hand"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A **heap** is a structure giving fast access to the smallest element. `heapq` works on plain lists: `heappush` adds, `heappop` ALWAYS removes the smallest."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import heapq",
          "h = []",
          "heapq.heappush(h, 3)",
          "heapq.heappush(h, 1)",
          "heapq.heappush(h, 2)",
          "print(heapq.heappop(h))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`heapq.nsmallest(n, data)` and `nlargest(n, data)` give the n smallest/largest without sorting everything."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "A heap underlies a priority queue: always handle the most urgent thing first."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m60l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `ordenar_heap(nums)` que ordene metiendo todo en un heap y sacándolo (heappush/heappop).",
        "en": "Define `ordenar_heap(nums)` sorting by pushing everything into a heap and popping it out."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def ordenar_heap(nums):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def ordenar_heap(nums):",
        "    h = []",
        "    for n in nums:",
        "        heapq.heappush(h, n)",
        "    return [heapq.heappop(h) for _ in range(len(h))]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Empuja todos y luego saca tantos como haya."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Push all then pop as many as there are."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "ordenar_heap",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  3,
                  1,
                  2
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                1,
                2,
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  5,
                  5,
                  1
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                1,
                5,
                5
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                []
              ],
              "expected": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m60l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `n_menores(nums, n)` que devuelva los n valores más pequeños (usa heapq.nsmallest).",
        "en": "Define `n_menores(nums, n)` returning the n smallest values (use heapq.nsmallest)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def n_menores(nums, n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def n_menores(nums, n):",
        "    return heapq.nsmallest(n, nums)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "heapq.nsmallest(n, nums)."
        ],
        "en": [
          "heapq.nsmallest(n, nums)."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "n_menores",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  5,
                  1,
                  8,
                  3
                ],
                2
              ],
              "expected": [
                1,
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  4,
                  4,
                  4
                ],
                2
              ],
              "expected": [
                4,
                4
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}